<BaseLayout title="About | Trace & Triage">

<p class="case-id">ABOUT</p>

<h1>About Trace & Triage</h1>

<p>
  I work within Digital Forensics and eDiscovery and have
  a wider interest in incident response, malware analysis,
  cybersecurity and emerging forms of digital evidence.
</p>

<p>
  Trace & Triage is my personal research journal documenting
  practical investigations conducted within controlled,
  isolated or otherwise authorised environments.
</p>


<h2>Research Interests</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Digital Forensics</li>
  <li>Incident Response</li>
  <li>Malware Analysis</li>
  <li>Threat Hunting</li>
  <li>Security Operations</li>
  <li>Drone Forensics</li>
  <li>Vehicle Forensics</li>
  <li>Mobile Forensics</li>
  <li>Satellite & Space Cybersecurity</li>
</ul>


<h2>Research Philosophy</h2>

<p>
  My aim is to understand not only how security events occur,
  but what evidence they leave behind and how that evidence
  can be used to reconstruct activity.
</p>


<h2>Disclaimer</h2>

<p>
  Research and opinions published on Trace & Triage are my own
  and do not represent my employer.
</p>

<p>
  All security testing and malware analysis is performed within
  isolated or authorised environments. Client, confidential,
  classified and employer information is never published.
</p>

